# Paths that exist only in this fork and never go upstream. One per line, relative to the
# repo root; a directory covers everything under it. derive-pr.py removes these from the
# derive BEFORE anything else looks at it, so they cannot ride along in a pull request, and
# it refuses a --paths entry that names one of them.
#
# Add a line here in the same commit that adds a fork-only file. A fork-only file missing
# from this list is still caught, but later and less kindly: as a stray path outside --paths,
# or by the tripwire that refuses a worker_log.md or handoff.md anywhere in the tree.
worker_log.md
handoff.md
AGENTS.md
.gitattributes
tools/upstream
